# Insights homepage cards

Homepage “latest insights” come from `src/data/latestInsights.generated.ts`, written by `scripts/sync-published-routes.mjs`. The homepage renders them as tabs: **All**, **System Design**, **Under the Hood** (`latestInsightsByTab`), up to 8 cards each.

## Tab behavior (important)

- **All tab** = curated strip. Respects both `draft: true` and `homepage: false`.
- **Series tabs** (`system-design`, `under-the-hood`) = latest posts carrying that topic tag. They **exclude drafts** but **include `homepage: false`** posts. This is deliberate: `homepage: false` keeps a post off the flat All strip, while still letting it surface under its dedicated series tab.
- `latestInsights` remains exported as an alias of the All tab for back-compat.

## Do not put these on the homepage

1. **Drafts** (`draft: true`) — never appear in any tab. The sync script skips them even if you pass `--include-drafts`.
2. **Under the Hood (Internet foundations) series** and any insight that should stay off the flat All strip — set:

```yaml
homepage: false
```

Use for: DNS / CDN / Anycast / TCP vs UDP Under the Hood (and similar primers meant for dig/series reading, not All-strip promotion). Note: with `homepage: false` these still appear under the **Under the Hood** tab if tagged `under-the-hood`.

## Agent rules

- When creating or editing Under the Hood Internet-foundations insights, include `homepage: false` in frontmatter (alongside `draft: true` until published).
- Do **not** expect `--include-drafts` to preview those cards on the homepage. It may still refresh other published-route data; the All tab stays published-only and respects `homepage: false`.
- After insight create/rename, run `node scripts/sync-published-routes.mjs` (add `--include-drafts` only if you need draft routes elsewhere). Confirm new Under the Hood slugs are **absent** from the `all` tab in `latestInsights.generated.ts` (they may appear under the `under-the-hood` tab).
- Do not hand-edit `latestInsights.generated.ts` to force a draft onto the homepage.

